course: dictionary
lesson: 16032
title: Word for word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Verbatim means in exactly the same words as were used at first, word for word. Nothing is changed, not even one small word.
explain: «Please repeat the rule verbatim» means say the rule with exactly the same words it had before. If you change even one word, you are no longer repeating it verbatim.
explain: When you copy from a book or a website, you must say where the words came from. If you quote verbatim, put the words in quotation marks and name the source.
fact: Verbatim means word for word, in exactly the same words.
fact: «Quote verbatim» means copy the words exactly and put them in quotation marks.
fact: «A verbatim copy» is an exact copy of the original, with nothing changed.
fact: Copying a website verbatim into your project without saying where it came from is plagiarism.
fact: In law and news, a verbatim record is an exact copy of what was said.
exercise: «Please repeat the rule verbatim, so the whole class hears the exact words.» What does verbatim mean? | Said with a funny voice | Shortened and made simpler | *Word for word, in exactly the same words | Written in a hurry
exercise: «She quoted the poem verbatim and put it in quotation marks.» Which phrase shows she copied it exactly? | She forgot the poem | *She quoted the poem verbatim | She told the poem in her own words | She drew a picture of the poem
exercise: Ben copies a whole paragraph from a website into his project and does not name it. What is wrong? | The paragraph is too long to read | *It is plagiarism, because he did not say where the words came from | Nothing, because copying is always fine | The paragraph is too short to count
test: Which is a verbatim copy? | A summary written in your own words | A copy with some pictures added | A copy with a new title at the top | *A copy with every word exactly the same as the original
test: Ella writes the idea in her own words and says it is verbatim. Is she right? | Yes, because her writing is shorter | *No, verbatim means the exact same words | Yes, because she kept the same meaning | Yes, because she did it in class
exam: «The notice said: Keep off the grass, and Sam repeated it verbatim.» What does verbatim mean in this sentence? | Turning it into a question | Shouting loudly | *Using the exact same words | Using different words with the same meaning
